{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 89, :comments ["<b>The voice speaking to him.</b> According to what we have written in other places (Exodus 20:1), that the utterance going forth from HaShem would be fashioned from it an angel, and it is the one speaking to the prophet — and on this basis I have explained every instance of the word לֵאמֹר (\"to say\") that appears in the words of HaShem. And this is what it says, <b>the voice speaking to him</b> — meaning, the voice of the Holy One, blessed be He, speaks to him. And even though the word is pointed with a dagesh as though it were מִתְדַּבֵּר (being spoken), since the voice itself is the utterance, it is justified to be said in this manner. And the discerning one will understand." "<b>Thus is concluded the section of Naso.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:49.614396830Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}